data.discoveries:
Achieved the first soft touchdown on a comet nucleus;
COSAC gas chromatograph identified 16 organic compounds including four nitrogen-bearing molecules (methyl isocyanate, acetone, propionaldehyde, and acetamide) never before seen on comets;
MUPUS hammer penetrator proved the cometary ice-dust crust beneath the surface dust layer was as hard as solid rock (tensile strength >2 MPa);
ROMAP magnetometer confirmed the comet nucleus is completely unmagnetized.

Discovered active sulfur volcanism on Jupiter’s moon Io (the first active volcanism confirmed beyond Earth);
Discovered two new moons of Jupiter (Thebe and Metis) and a faint Jovian ring system;
Discovered five new moons of Saturn and revealed intricate ringlet structures;
Captured the legendary 'Pale Blue Dot' portrait of Earth from 6 billion km away;
Detected the sharp boundary of the Heliopause and measured the density of interstellar plasma directly.

Discovered 90% pure opaline silica soils churned up by its frozen right-front wheel, proving past volcanic hydrothermal fumaroles or hot springs;
Discovered iron-magnesium carbonate outcrops at Comanche, proving an ancient neutral-pH water environment under a thick carbon-dioxide atmosphere;
Scaled Husband Hill summit (107 meters elevation).

Discovered hematite-rich spherules ('Martian blueberries') proving past standing acidic water;
Uncovered sulfate mineral veins in Endeavour Crater indicating neutral-pH ancient water;
Completed the first off-world marathon distance (42.195 km) in March 2015;
Explored Eagle, Endurance, Victoria, and Endeavour craters revealing vast stratified geological records.

Enabled astronauts to climb the slopes of Mt. Hadley Delta and discover the 'Genesis Rock' (Sample 15415, anorthosite dated to 4.1 billion years, confirming the lunar magma ocean hypothesis);
Collected 77 kg of lunar rock and soil samples;
Explored the 300-meter-deep chasm of Hadley Rille.

Measured the temperature profile of lunar topsoil using the ChaSTE thermal probe, discovering a dramatic 60°C gradient between the surface (~50°C) and just 8 cm below (-10°C);
Recorded lunar seismic activity using the ILSA seismometer, including signals from rover movement and micro-meteoroid impacts;
Demonstrated in-situ engine re-ignition and a 40-centimeter hop test essential for future sample return missions.

Unambiguously confirmed the presence of Sulfur (S) in the high southern lunar regolith using the Laser-Induced Breakdown Spectroscope (LIBS);
Detected aluminum, calcium, iron, chromium, titanium, manganese, silicon, and oxygen;
Traversed 101.4 meters while navigating around obstacles including a 4-meter-diameter crater.

ROSINA spectrometer determined that the deuterium-to-hydrogen (D/H) ratio in comet 67P’s water vapor is three times greater than that of Earth’s oceans, showing comets of this family were not the primary source of Earth’s water;
Discovered glycine (an amino acid) and phosphorus (key to DNA/cell membranes) in the comet coma;
Discovered molecular oxygen (O2) outgassing in high abundances (~3.8% relative to water);
Mapped the duck-shaped bilobate nucleus structure.
